      "writtenOn": "2026-11-06T15:20:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`__PKVM_HYP__` is a x86-specific macro, while this is generic code. (FWIW, ARM\u0027s counterpart is `__KVM_NVHE_HYPERVISOR__`, though it is used to a much lesser extent than we currently use `__PKVM_HYP__` on x86.)\n\nSo this could be e.g. `#if defined(CONFIG_PKVM_X86) \u0026\u0026 defined(__PKVM_HYP__)` (even uglier, but explicit)?\n\n...Besides, since this is generic kernel code, not x86 KVM or IOMMU specific, we shouldn\u0027t merge this without an approval from Android kernel team. (_If_ we really have no choice but merge this at all...)",
      "revId": "accc167fec7f3476dcbc6233fedb39dce8aeb71c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
