      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-06T15:20:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you are considering upstreaming such a refactoring right away, I\u0027m wondering what would be the justification for it, if it is only needed downstream.\n\nIf you are considering keeping such a refactoring out of tree, that would make it difficult to resolve conflicts when rebasing onto newer upstream kernels and when applying bugfixes from upstream? (For these reasons, we deliberately prefer to keep this ugly sprinkling of ifdefs throughout arch/x86/kvm/ and drivers/iommu/intel/ instead of heavy reshuffling of upstream code, so long as our changes remain out of tree.)",
